{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795255325,"nonce":"ax29MQaxhwzzVbNNUTAPztWQ7Qw=","title":"Keep DistanceSpeed's window at 10 s for fast-reporting treadmills","message":"Found in the repo audit, 2026-11-21. Low priority: no treadmill seen so far needs it.\n\nengine::speed::DistanceSpeed averages total distance over DISTANCE_WINDOW_MS (10 s), but its\nDeque holds only 16 samples. A distance-only treadmill sending 2 records/s gets an 8 s window, 4/s\ngets 4 s (0.9 km/h steps at 1 m resolution, a jumpy pace), and above 8/s the samples never span\nMIN_SPAN_MS, so the watch always gets 0.\n\nFix: overwrite the newest sample instead of pushing when it is under about 625 ms old, so 16\nsamples always cover 10 s.\n\nTest in speed.rs: 10 samples/s at a steady speed for 15 s gives that speed.","files":null}]}